  "name": "CRYPTOSPORIDIUM ANTIGEN DETECTION STOOL",
  "code": "2720",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"55\" data-end=\"379\">The <strong data-start=\"59\" data-end=\"91\">Cryptosporidium antigen test</strong> is a <strong data-start=\"97\" data-end=\"112\">stool-based</strong> diagnostic test used to detect <strong data-start=\"144\" data-end=\"163\">Cryptosporidium</strong> antigens. It is a <strong data-start=\"182\" data-end=\"215\">highly sensitive and specific</strong> method for identifying infections caused by <em data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"284\">Cryptosporidium parvum</em> and <em data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"314\">Cryptosporidium hominis</em>, which are protozoan parasites that cause <strong data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"378\">cryptosporidiosis</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1284\" data-end=\"1313\"><strong data-start=\"1288\" data-end=\"1313\">Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1315\" data-end=\"1596\">\n<li data-start=\"1315\" data-end=\"1394\">\n<p data-start=\"1317\" data-end=\"1394\">A <strong data-start=\"1319\" data-end=\"1338\">positive result</strong> confirms infection and helps guide treatment decisions.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1395\" data-end=\"1470\">\n<p data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1470\">In <strong data-start=\"1400\" data-end=\"1431\">immunocompetent individuals</strong>, the infection is often self-limiting.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1596\">\n<p data-start=\"1473\" data-end=\"1596\">In <strong data-start=\"1476\" data-end=\"1506\">immunocompromised patients</strong>, the disease may be severe and prolonged, requiring targeted therapy and supportive care.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive</strong></td>\n<td>Cryptosporidium antigen is detected. Indicates <strong>current infection</strong> with Cryptosporidium.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative</strong></td>\n<td>No antigen detected. Either no infection, or the parasite is below detection levels. Consider repeat testing if suspicion is high.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
